+# Fossil Gen 6 (fossil-hoki) Mainline Target
+
+## Device Specifications
+- **Manufacturer:** Fossil
+- **Model:** Gen 6
+- **Codename:** `fossil-hoki` / `hoki`
+- **SoC:** Qualcomm Snapdragon Wear 4100+ (`SDA429W` / `SDM429W`, 4x Cortex-A53)
+- **GPU:** Qualcomm Adreno 504
+- **Display:** 416 x 416 circular AMOLED (1.28")
+- **Memory / Storage:** 1GB RAM / 8GB eMMC
+
+## Mainline Bring-up References
+- **Nura / postmarketOS Wiki:** [Fossil Gen 6 (fossil-hoki)](https://wiki.nura.eco/wiki/Fossil_Gen_6_(fossil-hoki))
+- **Mainline Linux Kernel PR:** [msm89x7-mainline/linux#29 (arm64: dts: qcom: Add SDM429)](https://github.com/msm89x7-mainline/linux/pull/29)
+- **lk2nd Bootloader PR:** [msm8916-mainline/lk2nd#552 (dts: msm8952: add support for Fossil Gen 6)](https://github.com/msm8916-mainline/lk2nd/pull/552)
+- **postmarketOS Integration:** [pmaports!6809](https://gitlab.postmarketos.org/postmarketOS/pmaports/-/merge_requests/6809)
+
+## Hardware & Subsystem Details
+- **Display:** Handled via continuous splash `simple-framebuffer` at base `0x90001000`:
+  - Resolution: 416 x 416
+  - Pixel format: `r8g8b8` (24-bit RGB)
+  - Stride: 1248 bytes (`416 * 3`)
+  - Reserved memory: `0x90001000`, size `0x7ec00`, marked `no-map`.
+- **Buttons / Input:**
+  - Volume Up (`KEY_VOLUMEUP`): GPIO 35 (`TLMM 35`, active low with pull-up).
+  - Volume Down (`KEY_VOLUMEDOWN`): PMIC PON resin pin (`&pon_resin`).
+  - Power (`KEY_POWER`): PMIC PON pwrkey (`&pon_pwrkey`).
+- **Storage:** eMMC on SDHC1 (`7824900.sdhci`), powered by RPM PM660 regulators `pm660_l19` (`vmmc`) and `pm660_l13` (`vqmmc`).
+- **USB:** High-speed USB in peripheral mode (`dr_mode = "peripheral"`) with extcon dummy and PM660 regulators (`l6`, `l12`, `l16`).
+- **Haptics & Battery:** Managed by PM660 SPMI PMIC (`pm660_haptics`, `pm660_fg`, `pm660_charger`).
+
+## Fastboot & Flashing Instructions
+1. **Enter Fastboot mode:**
+   - Power off the watch completely.
+   - Hold down **all three physical buttons** simultaneously until the fastboot screen appears.
+2. **Flash Mainline Image:**
+   ```bash
+   fastboot flash boot boot.img
+   fastboot flash userdata system.img
+   fastboot reboot
+   ```
+3. **Dualbooting with AsteroidOS (from Nura Wiki):**
+   - AsteroidOS rootfs is placed on the `system` partition.
+   - AsteroidOS kernel is placed on the `recovery` partition.
+   - Mainline rootfs is placed on the `userdata` partition.
+   - When using `lk2nd` secondary bootloader, flash a dummy DTBO image (`dtbo-fossil-hoki.img`) to `dtbo`.
